[[0,2014554,0,1,0,1,"2017-07-24T01:15:41","probsgonnabedead","",[],"<p>all</p>\n<p>back in 2016, someone here, filed a foiapa request with the fbi that was given request number 1361582-000. the subject of this request was fbi documents discussing symbolism within pedophilia organizations.</p>\n<p>i have been checking this request for a number of months and it always said pending, however, as of recently, the fbi fault and fbi foia office say that this request does not exist or the request number is not valid.</p>\n<p>has anyone else experienced instances of valid foiapa cases suddenly disappearing as appears to be the case here? is there any remedial action that can be taken? and is there any similar foia responses or documents regarding the requested subject matter?</p>","FBI - FOIAPA: 1361582-000","","pizzagate"],[1,9937691,0,0,0,0,"2017-07-24T02:00:47","gumshoe_mob","",[],"<p>On the left of the page of this FOIA request is an example of an assigned tracking number for such FOIA requests.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.muckrock.com/foi/united-states-of-america-10/cybersecurity-task-force-past-and-present-documents-16326/\">https://www.muckrock.com/foi/united-states-of-america-10/cybersecurity-task-force-past-and-present-documents-16326/</a></p>"],[1,9942583,0,0,0,0,"2017-07-24T18:14:43","Blowitwideopen","",[],"<p>And have you been in contact with original poster? To make sure they are still valid?</p>"]]
